# The site builds with no environment variable at all: it is a static export
# with no server, no secrets and nothing to log in to. One variable is read
# when it is set.

# Google Search Console's verification token for hivefleet.dev (the content of
# the "HTML tag" method, without the tag around it). When set, every page
# carries <meta name="google-site-verification" content="...">; when empty,
# nothing is added. It is public by nature: it is printed in the page. Set it
# in the Vercel project's environment for production, or in .env.local here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=
